---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const snippet = `<iframe src="${SITE.url}/embed" title="CTC to in-hand salary calculator" width="100%" height="840" style="border:0;max-width:560px" loading="lazy"></iframe>
<p><a href="${SITE.url}/">CTC to in-hand salary calculator</a> by ${SITE.name}</p>`;
---

<DocLayout
  title="Embed the calculator on your site"
  description={`Add a free CTC to in-hand salary calculator to your blog or HR site. One snippet, both tax regimes, ${SITE.shortYearLabel} rates, kept up to date for you.`}
  updated="2026-10-04"
>
  <p>
    If you write about salaries, offers or payroll, you can put a working CTC calculator on your own
    page. It uses the same engine as this site, compares both tax regimes and applies your reader's
    state professional tax. When the law changes, the embedded calculator updates on its own.
  </p>

  <h2>The snippet</h2>
  <p>Paste this where you want the calculator to appear:</p>
  <pre
    class="overflow-x-auto rounded-sm bg-sunken p-4 text-xs leading-5 text-ink"
    tabindex="0"
    aria-label="Embed snippet"
  ><code id="embed-snippet">{snippet}</code></pre>
  <p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-copy-snippet>
      Copy the snippet
    </button>
  </p>
  <p>
    Add <code>?theme=dark</code> or <code>?theme=light</code> to the address to fix the colour
    scheme; otherwise it follows your reader's system setting. In a column narrower than 400px,
    raise the height to about 920.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. Please keep the credit line under the calculator: it is how people find the full
    breakdown, and how we keep this free. The calculator collects nothing, sets no cookies and sends
    nothing anywhere; everything is worked out in your reader's browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Preview</h2>
  <iframe
    src="/embed"
    title="CTC to in-hand salary calculator"
    width="100%"
    height="840"
    style="border:0;max-width:560px"
    loading="lazy"
  ></iframe>
</DocLayout>

<script>
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-snippet]');
  const code = document.getElementById('embed-snippet');
  button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const text = code?.textContent ?? '';
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
      button.textContent = 'Copied';
    } catch {
      window.prompt('Copy the snippet', text);
    }
    window.setTimeout(() => (button.textContent = 'Copy the snippet'), 2000);
  });
</script>
